# Cargo build output. Un-anchored on purpose: `bins/opc-gui/` and
# `bins/opc-tray/` each carry their own out-of-workspace Cargo.lock and
# are built standalone by release.yml, so nested `target/` dirs are
# routine here. The old root-anchored `/target` plus hand-written
# per-crate rules is how 710 blobs of Windows build output ended up in
# this repo's history.
target/
# Alternate cargo target directory used when the primary `target/`
# is locked by a stuck child opc.exe (kernel-mode wait on Wintun).
# Root-only, unlike `target/` — nothing nests this one.
/target-fresh
# Manual downloads of prior releases for diff inspection — not part
# of the source tree.
/release
**/*.rs.bk
.vscode/
.idea/
.direnv/
.envrc
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store
.claude/
*.dSYM/

# Project-internal docs that should not be public.
CLAUDE.md
/_refs/

# Dev-tool session marker (dropped by external CLI tooling).
.codex

# Secrets / runtime artifacts.
#
# Anything matching the credential globs below is assumed to be a real
# secret. Synthetic test material lives under `tests/fixtures/` and is
# re-admitted at the end of this block, so a self-signed fixture cert
# for the client-certificate work can actually be committed instead of
# silently failing to stage.
.env
.env.*
*.log
*.token
*.pem
*.key
*.cer
*.crt
*.der
*.p12
*.pfx
# The user's runtime profile. Anchored: a bare `config.toml` also
# matches `.cargo/config.toml`, which this repo has a real use for
# (per-target `[env]` for OPENCONNECT_DIR / LIBCLANG_PATH).
/config.toml
# `gp_config::Config::save_to` writes `<path>.tmp` and renames; the
# temp file lands in the CWD when `ProjectDirs` is unavailable, and it
# holds the portal URL, username and Okta tenant.
/config.toml.tmp
/run/

# Live-test log dump.
/.opc-logs/
.session-archives/

# Local reproductions of the release packaging steps, which all run in
# the checkout root and would otherwise land next to a `git add -A`.
/dist/
/dll-cache/
/wintun.zip
/wintun-extract/
/openprotect-cli-*/
/openprotect-gui-*/
openprotect-*.tar.gz
openprotect-*.zip
# Dropped in the package CWD by resolve_hip_script_accepts_relative_path
# when it panics before its cleanup.
opc-hip-rel-test-*.sh

# Test fixtures are synthetic by policy, so they must stay committable
# even when they match a credential glob above.
!**/tests/fixtures/**
